\f1\fs22 Hayley followed Eloise, and the farther she followed, the less she understood about the function and intent of the bunker. What she thought was a living space where she left everyone else, she reframed as a reception space, and the bedroom suite corridor was for guests Eloise might not want in deeper parts of the bunker. There may have been dedicated residential spaces, but Hayley had no sense of where they might be; during the extended walk to the security functions, Hayley\'92s comprehension of the complex was reduced to a catalogue of observations: offices; artworks; a conference space; wide corridors; staircases; comfortable lighting; good air; discreet signage on walls and doors; fire extinguishers in discrete, recessed cabinets, and\'97what the tax?\'97a water feature. There could have been a gymnasium, a movie theatre and high street shopping district, for all Hayley knew.\
